course: dictionary
lesson: 11926
title: Judging words: callous
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Callous is a judging word. It describes someone who is cruel and does not care when other people feel hurt or sad. «He laughed when the new boy fell over, and he did not even ask if he was OK.» The clues are laughed and did not ask: a callous person shows no pity.
explain: Look for the feeling behind the action. Callous can describe a person, an action or a remark. «It was a callous remark to tell her that nobody would miss her.» The words show no care for her feelings at all.
explain: Its opposites are kind, caring and compassionate. To check your meaning, swap in a kind word, such as «It was a kind remark to tell her that everyone would miss her.» If the sentence now sounds nice instead of cruel, callous must mean the unkind opposite.
fact: Callous means cruel and not caring about other people's feelings or pain.
fact: «Callous» can describe a person, an action or a remark, as in «a callous remark».
fact: You may meet phrases like callous behaviour, callous disregard and callous indifference.
fact: The opposites of callous are kind, caring and compassionate.
fact: Callous is a strong word, so use it for behaviour that really hurts people.
exercise: «He laughed at the hurt puppy and walked past without helping.» What does callous suggest? | *Cruel and not caring | Tired and sleepy | Happy and playful | Very clever
exercise: Which word means the opposite of callous? | Rude | *Kind | Cruel | Loud
exercise: Which is the best meaning of callous? | *Cruel and not caring about other people's pain | Kind and gentle | Full of energy | Very loud and noisy
test: «The callous woman left her neighbour's dog out in the rain and laughed.» What does callous mean here? | *Cruel and showing no pity | Kind and careful | Tired after a long day | Happy and smiling
test: Which sentence shows a callous remark? | *«Nobody cares if you cry, so stop being a baby.» | «Well done, you tried so hard!» | «Shall we share the cake?» | «Let's help the lost kitten.»
exam: Ben says, «Callous means very kind.» Why is he wrong? | *Callous means cruel and not caring, the opposite of kind | Callous means happy | Callous means very kind and gentle | Callous means quiet
